Subject: [PATCH] speech: TTS voices from the profile, with timed utterances

speechSynthesis.getVoices() lists the voices in the profile's
speech.voices, and these replace the host's voices. On a Linux host
without speech-dispatcher the list is otherwise empty, which no real
desktop reports. When no real synthesizer is running, speak() fires
start and end events after the time real speech would take, about
fifteen characters a second scaled by the rate, with no audio. Patch
0043 removes this timer and keeps only voices a real provider registers.

diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.h b/base/apostate/profile.h
index 52bd72f..82ecce0 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.h
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <set>
 #include <optional>
 #include <string>
+#include <vector>
 
 #include "base/base_export.h"
 
@@ -288,6 +289,25 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
     return hw_decode_codecs_;
   }
 
+  // One speech-synthesis voice as speechSynthesis.getVoices() reports it.
+  struct SpeechVoice {
+    std::string name;
+    std::string lang;
+    bool is_default = false;
+  };
+
+  // The claimed machine's TTS voices.
+  //
+  // An empty list is a strong container tell: every real desktop has voices,
+  // Windows ships around twenty SAPI ones, and a Linux box without
+  // speech-dispatcher installed reports none at all. The list is also
+  // platform-shaped rather than arbitrary — "Microsoft Hazel - English (United
+  // Kingdom)" is not a name any other OS produces — so it has to be replayed
+  // rather than invented.
+  const std::vector<SpeechVoice>& speech_voices() const {
+    return speech_voices_;
+  }
+
   // IANA timezone name, e.g. "Europe/Warsaw".
   //
   // Only the zone *name* is a host fact. ICU's data is compiled into the binary
@@ -377,6 +397,7 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   std::map<std::string, SystemFont> css_system_fonts_;
   std::optional<bool> screen_is_extended_;
   std::set<std::string> hw_decode_codecs_;
+  std::vector<SpeechVoice> speech_voices_;
   std::optional<std::string> timezone_;
   std::optional<bool> prefers_dark_;
   std::optional<std::string> accept_languages_;
